mkitem!{mkstruct!{# [doc = " Used for emitting structured error messages and other diagnostic information."] # [doc = " Wraps a `DiagInner`, adding some useful things."] # [doc = " - The `dcx` field, allowing it to (a) emit itself, and (b) do a drop check"] # [doc = "   that it has been emitted or cancelled."] # [doc = " - The `EmissionGuarantee`, which determines the type returned from `emit`."] # [doc = ""] # [doc = " Each constructed `Diag` must be consumed by a function such as `emit`,"] # [doc = " `cancel`, `delay_as_bug`, or `into_diag`. A panic occurs if a `Diag`"] # [doc = " is dropped without being consumed by one of these functions."] # [doc = ""] # [doc = " If there is some state in a downstream crate you would like to access in"] # [doc = " the methods of `Diag` here, consider extending `DiagCtxtFlags`."] # [must_use] pub struct Diag < 'a , G : EmissionGuarantee = ErrorGuaranteed > { pub dcx : DiagCtxtHandle < 'a > , # [doc = " Why the `Option`? It is always `Some` until the `Diag` is consumed via"] # [doc = " `emit`, `cancel`, etc. At that point it is consumed and replaced with"] # [doc = " `None`. Then `drop` checks that it is `None`; if not, it panics because"] # [doc = " a diagnostic was built but not used."] # [doc = ""] # [doc = " Why the Box? `DiagInner` is a large type, and `Diag` is often used as a"] # [doc = " return value, especially within the frequently-used `PResult` type. In"] # [doc = " theory, return value optimization (RVO) should avoid unnecessary"] # [doc = " copying. In practice, it does not (at the time of writing)."] diag : Option < Box < DiagInner > > , _marker : PhantomData < G > , }}}
